{
  "_about": "Ships at sea (sea step 5a). The SWIFT stage (sea step 5e, Sailing unlock at sailing_level): the wind always counts as blowing from astern (the best share of wind_efficiency), at least wind_at_least of a full wind, times speed_mult; only a helmsman with that Sailing level can set it. Director: ship-local decks (players walk the rolling deck), a WORLD FLEET (ships belong to the host's world and stay where left), Valheim wind with sail settings, the HELMSMAN'S Sailing level gates the ship tier and his perks apply. stages: what W / S step through at the helm (sail 0..1 of the wind's push, oars m/s without wind, negative = backwards). wind_efficiency: [degrees off the wind, share of the push]; 0 = the wind straight from behind, 180 = straight into it (no way forward on sail). wind_floor: the push at no wind (0) .. full at wind 1. Per ship (all sizes metres, ship space: x starboard, y up from the waterline, -z the bow): outline = half-widths of the deck along z (stern first), deck = deck height, draft = keel below the waterline, bulwark = rail height above the deck, top_speed m/s at full sail in the best wind, accel m/s per second, turn_deg per second at full way (turn_slow share at rest), sailing_level = the helmsman's Sailing level needed, xp_per_100m = Sailing xp for the helmsman per 100 m under sail, helm / anchor / mast = spots on deck, ladder_z = where the rope ladders hang over both sides, tilt = how far waves and wind may lean her. fleet: ships placed in the sea at the start (sea coordinates x, z, yaw degrees with 0 = bow to the north). ALL NUMBERS ARE MY PLACEHOLDERS. 5c (director: a SLIPWAY on region 1's test island now, the home port's dockyard later; SIDE SHIPS from FOUND PLANS; bigger ships = more CREW STATIONS): per ship also masts [[z, height], ...], sail = square / batten, steer = wheel / tiller, oar_mult (oars' strength), cannons = [[x, z], ...] cannon places for step 5d, rigging = [[x, z], ...] spots where a crew member holding interact trims the sails (rigging_bonus each while the sails are set), recipe = what the shipyard needs (data/fantasy/skilling.json recipes build_<id>), plan = the found plan the side ships need. shipyard: the slipway (sea coordinates, yaw), where its workbench stands (metres from the slipway along / across) and where a launched ship lies (launch m out to sea, spread m apart). Rework (director: walkable castles, each ship true to its type): levels = raised decks [{from, to (ship-space z), height above the main deck, stairs: [{x, low, high} = a ramp from the main deck at z low up to the level at z high]}]; spots on a level (helm, anchor, rigging) stand at its height.",
